<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Optus says talks with Seven still on.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Optus says talks with Seven still on.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telecommunications carrier Optus Communications Pty Ltd said on Tuesday that talks were still continuing with Seven Network Ltd to try to settlem litigation between Seven and Optus' pay-tv associate Optus Vision.</p>
<p>Earlier there were reports that the talks between the two camps had broken down. &quot;Talks are still continuing,&quot; Optus spokesman David Foster told Reuters. Foster said there was a deadline until 5 p.m. (0600 GMT) on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>Seven's started litigation against the Optus Vision shareholders -- Optus Communications, U.S. West Inc and Publishing and Broadcasting Ltd (PBL) -- after PBL was allowed to extend its option to raise its Optus Vision stake.</p>
<p>The court proceedings started just over a month ago between Seven and the Optus shareholders, but the two camps have been locked in settlement talks which could see the restructure of the Optus Vision ownership.</p>
<p>-- Kevin Morrison 61-2 9373-1813</p>
